   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Budgen</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>        	Perhaps you will have time to look over this before tonight. It is of course incorrect and incomplete <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">proof</seg>. Also the printer should have left a <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">gap</seg> after the <choice>
                            <sic>word</sic>
                            <corr>words</corr>
                        </choice> “looks on them” and before “Thanks eversore much”. The right <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">marginal comments</seg> and the left interchange. They start by being those of the master and the boys respectively. The footnotes are the girl’s.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>        	<name type="person" key="joyc82">J.J.</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Parts of what is now <name type="work">FW</name> II.2 were being typeset for publication as “Work in Progress: Opening and Closing Pages, Part II: Section II” in <name type="work">transition</name> no. 23 (July 1935).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">In what should have been a gap in the proofs, JJ intended to insert a manuscript section (“may all in the…culoteer”. <name type="work">FW</name> 274.13-275.02, BL MS 47478-235, 236; <name type="work">JJA</name> 52: 124-25). In relation to the gap, Harriet Shaw Weaver wrote “these two pages were sent to me later and do not appear in the typescript [§1.6/2.4/3A.6] made for <name type="work">transition</name> [no. 23, July 1935]. But they follow straight on after the 13th page of the fair copy and must have been inserted before <name type="work">transition</name> was printed” (<name type="work">JJA</name> 52: 121). Proofs for <name type="work">transition</name> no. 23 are missing; however the typescript ends with “looks on to the” (an earlier version of “looks on to that”) and fails to continue with “(may all in the tocoming)....Erin’s hircohaired culoteer”. (<name type="work">FW</name> 52:102).</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">This early arrangement, in what became <name type="work">FW</name> II.2, of the master’s marginal comments on one side and those of the boys on the other, changed at some point to the present arrangement of Shem’s comments on one side and Shaun’s on the other.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
